-- Rules that answer a list of n numbers whose end refuses, or raises a
-- division by zero, either as one more element or as the rest of the list.
-- A surface reads a list answer only so deep, so each case below is at the
-- last n whose end it reaches, or at the n one past it, where every surface
-- answers the list cut short. See boolean-rules.l4 for what an "agreement:"
-- line says, and for `pad`.
--
-- agreement: `refusal in the list` may refuse with ["deep"]
-- agreement: `refusal in the list` {"n": 200} => refuses "deep"
-- agreement: `refusal in the list` {"n": 201} => answers cut short
--
-- agreement: `refusal as the rest` may refuse with ["deep"]
-- agreement: `refusal as the rest` {"n": 201} => refuses "deep"
-- agreement: `refusal as the rest` {"n": 202} => answers cut short
--
-- agreement: `division in the list` may refuse with []
-- agreement: `division in the list` {"n": 200} => raises
-- agreement: `division in the list` {"n": 201} => answers cut short
--
-- agreement: `division as the rest` may refuse with []
-- agreement: `division as the rest` {"n": 201} => raises
-- agreement: `division as the rest` {"n": 202} => answers cut short
--
-- agreement: `refusal in a list of maybes` may refuse with ["deep"]
-- agreement: `refusal in a list of maybes` {"n": 199} => refuses "deep"
-- agreement: `refusal in a list of maybes` {"n": 200} => answers cut short

@export the numbers, then a refusal as one more element
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`refusal in the list` n pad MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN LIST (REFUSE "deep") ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `refusal in the list` (n MINUS 1) pad

@export the numbers, then a refusal as the rest of the list
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`refusal as the rest` n pad MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN REFUSE "deep" ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `refusal as the rest` (n MINUS 1) pad

@export the numbers, then a division by zero as one more element
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`division in the list` n pad MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN LIST (1 DIVIDED BY 0) ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `division in the list` (n MINUS 1) pad

@export the numbers, then a division by zero as the rest of the list
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`division as the rest` n pad MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN (IF 1 DIVIDED BY 0 EQUALS 0 THEN EMPTY ELSE EMPTY) ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `division as the rest` (n MINUS 1) pad

@export each number as a JUST, then a refusal as one more element
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
`refusal in a list of maybes` n pad MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN LIST (JUST (REFUSE "deep")) ELSE JUST n FOLLOWED BY `refusal in a list of maybes` (n MINUS 1) pad
